From d98ade4c9297ef35a1e30125951292055f552648 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:18:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] charging: optional Draine-Sutin Coulomb/image focusing for
 type-0 rates (default off)

Measurement switch for sec:charge / sec:moneyplot (charge_focusing_check_brief). The
type-0 grain-charging reactions use purely geometric rate coefficients, omitting the
Coulomb attraction of ions to negative grains and the image attraction of electrons to
neutral grains -- which is why the run comes out ~99% negative in every bin and inflates
the charge suppression of coagulation to a spurious ~11x.

- C1: two new parameters.in keys, read in read_parameters_in and written by the writer,
  defaulted in global_variables so an old parameters.in (lacking them) is bit-identical:
    charging_focusing (int, default 0): 0 keeps geometric rates bit for bit; 1 applies
      the focusing factors. electron_sticking (real, default 1.0): multiplies the e-
      attachment rate, applied only when charging_focusing = 1.
- C2: set_constant_rates type-0 loop, when charging_focusing = 1, multiplies each rate by
  the Draine & Sutin (1987) singly-charged closed form for this bin's reduced temperature
  tau_k = a_k k_B T_gas / e^2 (e = 4.80320471e-10 esu):
    electron onto neutral grain : s_e * (1 + sqrt(pi/(2 tau)))
    cation  onto negative grain : (1 + 1/tau)(1 + sqrt(2/(tau+2)))
  The projectile is identified from the reactants (e- = INDEL, or SPECIES_CHARGE = +1);
  a type-0 reaction matching neither aborts with an explicit message. No Jacobian change
  (the factor is abundance-independent; get_jacobian uses reaction_rates).

Verified: params_roundtrip ALL PASS; kernel-isolated gtodn_jac_fd_check byte-identical
with the switch on vs off (RESULT PASS, grain-col rel-err 3.7e-7); money-plot R0
(focusing=0) abundances.out byte-identical to the baseline binary; R0 charge metrics
reproduce the drafting-thread baseline exactly.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MZiMaHQmctaoPSEVjYonWi
